\section{Model Parameters}
\label{app:model_params}

For all experiments in Section~\ref{sec:experiments}, we use the same hyper parameters.
In particular, we consider the transductive setting, i.e., the train and test graphs are the same. Assuming access to node-labels, we obtain the hyperparameters of each model by means of Bayesian optimization.
The search space and obtained parameters for both the centralized and the federated settings are displayed in Table~\ref{tab:hyperparams}.

During model training, we employ the binary cross-entropy loss function, the ADAM optimizer, early stopping, a bath-size of $512$ and train for $300$ epochs.

