	\subsection{LoIU for Robot Team}

	Each robot updates its {operational status} and makes a decision within a time slot, e.g., through an appropriate design of time slot duration and the transmission schedules of the (collaborating) robots. In this way, $d_m^t$ is the overall delay for robot $m$ to update the operational status ${\bf X}_m^t$ in slot~$t$.
