\begin{equation}
    \label{A'}
    \boldsymbol{A}_{m}^{\prime}=\left\{a_{m}^{\prime}=\mu_{\theta_{m}^{{\mu}^{\prime} }}\left(o_{m}^{\prime}\right), \forall  o_{m}^{\prime} \in {\cal K}_m \right\} \in  \mathbb{R}^{K\times 2} \,. \\
\end{equation}
 The target critic network of the BS outputs a Q-value by inputting $\boldsymbol{o}^{\prime}$ %$\boldsymbol{o}^{w\prime}=\left\{o_1^{w\prime},\cdots,o_M^{w\prime}\right\}$ 
 from each sample $(\boldsymbol{o},\boldsymbol{a},\boldsymbol{r},\boldsymbol{o}^{\prime})$, and {$\boldsymbol{a}^{\prime}=\{a_{1}^{\prime},\cdots,a_{M}^{\prime}\}$} received from the robots. 

