    \field{sortinit}{H}
    \field{sortinithash}{H}
    \field{abstract}{%
    The application of the Petrov-Galerkin projection method in Cosserat rod
  finite element formulations offers significant advantages in simplifying the
  expressions within the discrete virtual work functionals. Moreover, it
  enables a straight-forward and systematic exchange of the ansatz functions,
  specifically for centerline positions and cross-section orientations. In this
  concise communication, we present a total Lagrangian finite element
  formulation for Cosserat rods that attempts to come up with the least
  required concepts. The chosen discretization preserves objectivity and allows
  for large displacements/rotations and for large strains. The orientation
  parametrization with non-unit quaternions results in a singularity-free
  formulation.%
    }
