    \field{abstract}{%
    Abstract In this paper, we introduce a new Reissner's geometrically exact
  beam element, which is based on a total Lagrangian updating procedure. The
  element has the rotation vector as the dependent variable and the singularity
  problems at the rotation angle 2{$\pi$} and its multiples are passed by the
  change of parametrization on the rotation manifold. The beam formulation has
  several benefits such as all the unknown vectors belong to the same
  tangential vector space, no need for secondary storage variables, the
  path-independence in the static case, any standard time-integration algorithm
  may be used, and the symmetric stiffness. Copyright {\copyright} 2006 John
  Wiley \& Sons, Ltd.%
