If the total reward function is defined as a linear function: $R_\omega(\{r_1, \dots, r_b\}) = \sum_{i=1}^{b}r_i\omega_i$ where $r_i$ indicates $i$-th sub-reward, then the preference is equal to the coefficients (importance factors) that we mentioned in the introduction.
