We show that these data are \textbf{Morita equivalent}, 
% More specifically, 
in the sense that we construct (a priori four) Boolean-ringed topoi from these four data and prove that they are equivalent. The author regards this as an example of Olivia Caramello's slogan of `toposes as bridges' (see \cite{caramello2023unification}), at least in a broader sense. This unified perspective demonstrates that the diverse views on regular languages can be interpreted as a single multifaceted topos.

