    \vspace{-10mm}
    \caption{\textbf{GAME's variants and ablations comparisons.} The solid line represents the median, and the shaded area shows the min and max of \num{3} replications over \num{20} generations. (a) \textbf{Diversity-only} and \textbf{GAME-SO} show the largest increase in solution size, but (b) \textbf{GAME-SO} shows the largest increase in complexity. (c-d) \textbf{Quality-only} and \textbf{GAME-MO (no VEM)} lead to the worst performances, while the others are similar. (e) Removing bootstrapping leads to a constant discovery of novel solutions. }
