\subsubsection{Multiple diagonals}
Besides courses with a single or a double-diagonal, there are also such that feature more than one diagonal pattern. There is often a centered “main” diagonal (which again can be a single or a double diagonal), as well as two (or sometimes more) further diagonals at the edges. These further diagonals are in most cases single diagonals. Such structures are often found in courses that adhere to a blended learning paradigm, where students are supposed to go through self-study units before the actual in-presence classes. The LMS course structure typically consists of a sequence of self-study units followed by the corresponding in-presence units. The typical patterns represent: a) trajectories from the current in-presence section to the next/previous in-presence section; b) movements from the current in-presence section to the next self-study section and c) from the current self-study section to the next in-presence section (see Fig. \ref{fig:multipl1}).

