When looking at the cross-course analysis (which as previously explained builds on data from 393 different Moodle courses) one can see that the \textit{typical} overall pattern for courses that are homogenized in the described way (and thus build on the blended learning paradigm) contains a dominant double diagonal and two further diagonals, together with a weaker pattern of a dominant section 1 (See Fig. \ref{fig:cross}).
