The double-diagonal indicates that students mostly navigate to the previous or next chapter, while the tendency to go forward to the next chapter is a bit stronger. The other diagonals indicate navigation from the in-presence sections to the respective self-study sections, and vice versa. From all sections, there is also a tendency to revisit the first section, especially from later in-presence sections and from the self study sections. 
