In order to minimize the maximum envy, we aim to determine an allocation $A$ that minimizes $MACC(G_{A,O})$. Given that there are $n!$ possible allocations, no known polynomial-time algorithm guarantees finding the optimal allocation. The existence of such an algorithm remains an open question.

