Note that for each $i \in N$, it holds that $\sum_{j\in N} w_{i,j} = 1$.

\begin{Remark}
    This model differs from the one presented in \cite{elmalem2025whoever}. Here, the values of the original apartments are subjective and may vary between agents. In contrast, if the values were objective—such as when determined by an appraiser—Elmalem et al.'s \cite{elmalem2025whoever} model would be applicable.
\end{Remark}

