\textbf{Inclusion Criteria:} Studies are included if they offer meaningful theoretical or empirical insights related to NLP, LLMs, and their application in software requirements. This includes topics like specification, formal logic, verification, and formal methods. 

\textbf{Exclusion Criteria:} Papers are excluded if they show in-sufficient relevance to the intersection of NLP/LLMs and software requirements, or if their abstracts or full texts lack sufficient detail. Non-peer-reviewed materials, duplicates, and items suggested by Elicit but deemed irrelevant after manual review are also removed.
